{"id": "EUVD-2026-81988", "enisaUuid": "5308cebc-1ed5-366e-9c9a-4c80253b7efb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphonet: pep: do not write beyond optlen in getsockopt\n\npep_getsockopt() clamps the reported length to the caller's buffer with\nmin_t(), but then stores the value with put_user(val, (int __user *)\noptval), which always writes sizeof(int) bytes. A getsockopt() call with\nan optlen smaller than sizeof(int) thus reports the clamped length yet\nwrites a full int, one to three bytes past the user buffer.\n\nWrite the value with copy_to_user() bounded by len, so at most optlen\nbytes are copied, matching the length reported back to userspace.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:01:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6054fed6bad08b6d03973e8ffca7f0c9394d1c30", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eac733a0b6fe0a52d91f9f623425735ed50ac6c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95e0ed2439dd1792eb454c68ae8d10f30ffe3bff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/056eea1a2068ad2fb7c3093c5f1095268f87d0c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bf499e438da80455e258049bce60ffb3a53f3fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4487e4d5309de587479ecc2f5173b49586f46f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f97022fefe6eb06ee18549d603420440f2959802", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77e5eb0e192aec6710c03ca8144582fd2af36ca4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j842-pq84-9gpj", "CVE-2026-90327"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04eaebdc-1571-3aa7-8d1d-6e51bfd06936", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "02a47617cdce440f60c71a51f3a93f9f5fcc5a7a <f97022fefe6eb06ee18549d603420440f2959802"}, {"id": "07a058e6-66a4-395b-9863-fd888a282489", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "07af377b-af85-3cca-a96b-43db8080f2fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "02a47617cdce440f60c71a51f3a93f9f5fcc5a7a <056eea1a2068ad2fb7c3093c5f1095268f87d0c7"}, {"id": "0aa73729-933c-35d5-9e63-a2c3fb9ff32c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "1e2f6640-66f8-30ce-86fb-cd20397129ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "02a47617cdce440f60c71a51f3a93f9f5fcc5a7a <77e5eb0e192aec6710c03ca8144582fd2af36ca4"}, {"id": "37c86518-777a-318e-8ca0-46dc10999946", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.28"}, {"id": "8dd7e31d-39e1-3e5d-8795-6272e73fa07f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8f7d32e8-f6e9-3b59-87c8-fcd713576781", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "909eed97-3c0f-3d59-9e9a-9332f5dc0af5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "02a47617cdce440f60c71a51f3a93f9f5fcc5a7a <1bf499e438da80455e258049bce60ffb3a53f3fa"}, {"id": "9154feb3-7f23-343b-a1e1-3008d5329d50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "98daed0c-1c09-34d2-946d-af9cda932618", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "a1c486bf-d2f6-3feb-8a5d-385888824cd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "02a47617cdce440f60c71a51f3a93f9f5fcc5a7a <c4487e4d5309de587479ecc2f5173b49586f46f4"}, {"id": "aea71226-7bb6-3005-b5e0-8a961bebc871", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "b11cb4ee-ebc6-3d36-ab22-cc1a95bc5d97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "02a47617cdce440f60c71a51f3a93f9f5fcc5a7a <6054fed6bad08b6d03973e8ffca7f0c9394d1c30"}, {"id": "be9d0bed-46a8-33a9-981d-3f505f823d04", "produ